40,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"My research reveals a lack of coordination. We are spending roughly 2,300 yen monthly on supplies, often buying duplicates. Furthermore, the management office's cleaning service costs 4,200 yen per hour, billed to a single tenant.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The time commitment is more significant than most realize. A full pass takes over an hour and a half. Additionally, an outside firm requires us to tidy beforehand, meaning outsourcing doesn't entirely remove the labor burden.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"My findings suggest a rather striking disparity. It appears that while we share the space, we do not share the usage; a few of us are the primary architects of the kitchen's chaos, while others are merely occasional visitors.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,1,talk,May,,"Wow, I found exactly what I suspected! We're all playing by different rules. Some people think ""done"" means a quick wipe, while others go full scrub. No wonder the rooms feel like a gamble every time I walk in!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I found something quite worrying in the previous tenants' note. They divided the rooms permanently, but by the second year, some of them barely spoke. I also noticed our chat rows start with reminders about undone chores.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Ryuji, if a full pass takes ninety minutes, the cost of professional cleaning is substantial. Combined with our inefficient supply spending, we are wasting both time and money. We need a system that tracks these expenses precisely.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Toshio, the cost is only one part of the problem. The real issue is the time. If we don't account for the full hour and a half, we'll simply end up with a system that feels unfair and overwhelming for whoever is on duty.","{""words"":44,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Ryuji, while I appreciate your focus on the clock, time is a relative currency. It is quite a curious tragedy to expect the same time commitment from someone who is barely a ghost in the hallways as from those of us who actually inhabit the space.","{""words"":46,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,2,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, you're so dramatic! But you're right—it's not just about the time, it's about the standard. If one person's ""clean"" is another person's ""grim,"" we're just waiting for the next fight to break out in the chat!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@May, that's exactly what I'm afraid of. If we just set a schedule without talking about our standards, the reminders will start again, and we might end up like the previous tenants who stopped speaking to each other.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Midori, your concern is valid, but standards are easier to align when the financial burden is transparent. We cannot ignore that supplies are being bought haphazardly and bills are currently landing on one person's shoulders.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Toshio, transparency in billing is useful, but it doesn't solve the labor issue. If the workload is underestimated, the financial system will be irrelevant because the person on duty will be too exhausted to follow it.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, @Ryuji, you both speak of transparency and labor as if they were separate entities. In reality, the most transparent system is one that acknowledges that usage and effort should be proportional. Why punish the ghost for the chef's mess?","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,3,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, you're making it sound like a courtroom drama! But seriously, if we just focus on who uses the kitchen more, we're still guessing about the bathroom. We need a clear, shared checklist so we stop the ""is it actually clean?"" lottery!","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@May, a checklist sounds like a wonderful idea! It would give us a shared language for what ""done"" means. I just hope we can implement it in a way that feels helpful rather than like we're policing each other.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"A checklist is a useful tool for standards, but it does not solve the financial instability. We must ensure that the cost of supplies and any professional services is split equitably and settled promptly to avoid resentment.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Toshio, financial stability is a given, but we must prioritize the time cost. If we don't establish a realistic time budget for these chores, the system will collapse regardless of how we split the bills. I'll be waiting for the options.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we are circling the drain of a classic dilemma: the battle between rigid equality and actual equity. I shall eagerly await the options, hoping they account for the fact that some of us are residents and others are mere tourists.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,2,4,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, you and your ""tourists""! Let's just hope the options give us a way to stop the guessing game. I'm ready to see if we can actually get a standard that doesn't end in a chat war!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
59,2,4,pass,May,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
60,2,4,talk,Midori,,"I agree with everyone. Whether it's the money, the time, or the standards, it all comes down to how we treat each other. I'm really hoping the options help us stay friends for the whole year!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
61,2,4,pass,Midori,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
