67,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Option B is the most logical choice. It eliminates the disputes over standards and the labor burden, while providing a clear, monthly invoice that ensures financial transparency and prevents any one person from being out of pocket.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option B is not as simple as it seems. My research showed that an outside firm requires us to tidy before they arrive. We would still be spending significant time preparing the rooms, meaning the labor burden isn't fully removed.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Option A is a recipe for a cold war. As Midori noted, the previous tenants tried permanent divisions and ended up in silence. It merely formalizes the disparity between the chef and the ghost.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,1,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, you're always thinking about the drama! But Option A is a total nightmare for me. If one person owns the bathroom and their ""clean"" is just a quick wipe, I'm stuck with that grimness forever! I can't live with that gamble.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,1,talk,Midori,,I agree with Benjamin. Option A sounds very risky since the previous tenants ended up not speaking to each other. I'm worried that permanent assignments would only lead to more resentment if someone feels their area is harder to maintain.,"{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Ryuji, the preparation time is a minor inconvenience compared to the current chaos. Option B provides a professional standard and a formal billing process, which is the only way to ensure that supply costs and service fees are settled fairly and promptly.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Toshio, it is not a minor inconvenience when it happens every week. If we still have to tidy and manage the arrival window, we are just paying a premium to shift the labor slightly. We need a solution that actually accounts for the hours.","{""words"":44,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, @Ryuji, your debate over the ""premium"" of professional cleaning is fascinating, yet it ignores the core issue. Option C is a rigid machine that treats a ghost and a chef as equals, which is a logical fallacy.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,2,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, stop trying to turn this into a philosophy class! Option C isn't a ""rigid machine,"" it's just a plan! At least with a rota, we can actually agree on a checklist so the state of the room doesn't change every single week!","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@May, I think you're right! A rota with a checklist would be much fairer than permanent spots. It lets us share the burden and ensures no one feels stuck with the hardest job for the whole year.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, your focus on usage is a separate issue from the necessity of a functioning system. Option C is prone to the same ""standard"" disputes May mentioned. Option B is the only one that guarantees a professional result and a clear financial trail.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Toshio, a professional result is useless if the preparation time still eats into our personal hours. Option C is the only choice that makes the time commitment explicit and shared, provided we use a checklist to keep the workload predictable.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, @Ryuji, you both seek a ""functioning system,"" yet you ignore that a system is only as fair as its inputs. Option C is a blind rotation that rewards the absent and punishes the present. It is a mathematical equality, not a moral one.","{""words"":44,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,3,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, you're just obsessed with who's a ""ghost"" and who's a ""chef""! I don't care who uses the kitchen more; I just want to know that when I walk into the bathroom, it's actually clean! Option C is the only way to keep us all accountable!","{""words"":46,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,3,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, I understand your point about usage, but I'm more worried about us staying on speaking terms. Option C feels like the kindest way to ensure no one feels singled out or burdened alone for too long.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
82,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"While Option C offers a shared burden, it does not address the financial instability of our supplies or the risk of one person funding the house. Option B is the only choice that ensures a professional standard and a transparent, settled invoice. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":47,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
83,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"Option B is a financial solution to a labor problem, but it doesn't actually eliminate the time cost. Option C is the only choice that makes the workload explicit and shared. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
84,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"It is a tragedy of logic that we must choose between a professional invoice and a blind rota. Since Option A is a social death sentence and Option B is a costly illusion, I shall vote for Option C. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":44,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
85,3,4,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, finally you've stopped the philosophy lecture! I'm with you and Ryuji on this one. Option C is the only way to stop the guessing game and keep us all in check. I vote for Option C!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
86,3,4,talk,Midori,,"I agree with the majority. While Option B is tempting for the quality, Option C is the most balanced way to share the effort and keep our spirits high. I vote for Option C!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
